 "about": "Unitree Dex1-1 at full opening: unitree_ros b579bbe, robots/g1_description/g1_29dof_mode_15_with_dex1_1.urdf (BSD-3-Clause): left_dex1_finger_joint_1/2 prismatic -0.02..0.0245 m, q 24.5 mm.  The body is Dex1_base_link.STL (the motor, the rails and the wrist adapter; not a closed surface, decimated all the same).  The Library mesh is Dex1_finger_link_1.STL; the other finger, Dex1_finger_link_2, is that finger turned 180 degrees about the approach axis (median 0.028 mm), so its sensor is the same board.  The looks: drawn after Unitree's product pictures of the Dex1-1 (unitree.com/Dex1-1 and the reseller copies of them: the only sharp views of every component) and after footage of the real gripper on the G1 (a factory clip, a lab clip, wrist-camera frames), 2026-11-12: a gripper black all over but for its two guide rails: the pebbled matt motor can, the satin block with its two carriages, the black-oxide pinion, the matt black alloy jaws (the Library's part: one mesh holding the jaw, its rubber pad, the UNITREE cover strip, the rack, the guide rail and the rail's end stop, so all of it wears the jaw's black).  A correction to the words above: the base link holds no rail; each finger's mesh holds its own guide rail and rack, which travel with the jaw, and the base link holds the two carriages and the pinion.  The bright steel is the project's own drawing, not the model's: on each finger plain boxes just proud of the rail and of the rack's body under it, with the rail's groove as a step (bodies/unitree-dex1/drawn-rail-sensor.stl and drawn-rail-mate.stl; the product pictures show both as one ground steel bar with dark teeth, which stay the mesh's), and the two black cap screws of the rail that stand outside the block at full opening, as plain discs over the mesh's counterbores, and with them a small black plate behind the one screw hole of the cover strip that stands outside the block, so that the drawn steel does not shine through the hole (drawn-rail-screws-sensor.stl, drawn-rail-screws-mate.stl).  Not modelled: every other screw (the meshes keep their holes), the pad's knurl and its rubber as a look of its own, the camera ring's bracket, the cable.",
